blocks.en:
score a text with a scoring model:
(1) Likelihood and Entropy, the mean token log-likelihood and entropy;
(2) DNA-GPT ( Yang et al., 2024 ) , the log-likelihood gap between the original continuation of a truncated text and K K regenerated ones;
(3) Fast-DetectGPT ( Bao et al., 2024 ) , the conditional probability curvature;
(4) Binoculars ( Hans et al., 2024 ) , the perplexity normalized by the cross-perplexity between two models;
(5) NTS ( Ma et al., 2026 ) , the normalized sensitivity of the token distribution to temperature.

blocks.zh:
以评分模式评分文本 :
(1) 可能值和Entropy, 平均符号对数的类似值和Entropy;
(2) DNA-GPT(Yang等人,2024年),截断文本的原延续与K K再生成文本之间的日志相似差距;
(3) 快速检测GPT (Bao等人,2024年),条件概率曲率;
(4) 双筒望远镜(Hans等人,2024年),由于两种型号的交叉性而使复杂度正常化;
(5)NTS(Ma等人,2026年),符号分布对温度的常态敏感度.

blocks.en:
are trained on labeled data:
(1) RoBERTa, a fine-tuned encoder classifier;
(2) RAIDAR ( Mao et al., 2024 ) , a multi-layer perceptron (MLP) on n-gram and edit-distance features between the text and its LLM rewrites;
(3) DPIC ( Yu et al., 2024 ) , a MLP on the embeddings of the text and of a response regenerated from its reconstructed prompt;
(4) ImBD ( Chen et al., 2025 ) , Fast-DetectGPT score under a fine-tuned scoring model with LoRA to prefer AI-generated style.

blocks.zh:
接受过标签数据培训:
(1) RoBERTA,经微调的编码器分类器;
(2) RAIDAR(Mao等人,2024年),在文本及其LLM重写之间的n-gm和编辑-距离特征上具有多层感官(MLP);
(3) DIC(Yu等人,2024年),在文本的嵌入和反应中重新生成的MLP;
(4)ImBD (Chen et al., 2025),快速检测GPT得分,在与LORA的微调评分模型下选择AI生成风格.
